ON DATA

This repository downloads no datasets and contains none. Everything it prints
is one of three things: arithmetic over published rates, a model defined and
labelled in the script that uses it, or - in 04_kubernetes - a measurement
taken from a Kubernetes cluster running on your own machine. No third-party
dataset licence applies to anything here.

ON SOFTWARE FETCHED AT RUNTIME

Nothing below is vendored in this repository. Each keeps its own licence, and
each is fetched from its publisher when you choose to run the thing that needs
it.

  PYTHON PACKAGES, via pip from requirements.txt
    matplotlib   (Matplotlib licence, BSD-compatible)
    numpy        (BSD 3-Clause)

  04_kubernetes/setup/install_kind.sh  DOWNLOADS, checksum-verified:
    kind         (Apache License 2.0) from github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kind
    kubectl      (Apache License 2.0) from dl.k8s.io
    Both versions are resolved at run time rather than pinned here.

  04_kubernetes/setup/install_docker_wsl.sh  ADDS Docker's apt repository
  and installs:
    Docker Engine and the compose/buildx plugins (Apache License 2.0)
    from download.docker.com. The script installs it; it does not
    redistribute it.

  04_kubernetes/kubernetes_live.py  causes CONTAINER IMAGES to be pulled:
    kindest/node       - a node image containing Kubernetes and containerd
                         (Apache License 2.0)
    nginx:1.27-alpine  - nginx (BSD 2-Clause) packaged as a Docker Official
                         Image, which carries its own terms

ON TOOLS THIS REPOSITORY DOES NOT USE

Two are worth stating plainly, because their names appear throughout and
their absence is deliberate:

  TERRAFORM is never invoked. 09_iac implements the documented graph
  ordering, three-way diff and force-new cascade rules itself, so that
  section runs with no Terraform binary and no credentials.

  THE GOOGLE CLOUD SDK (gcloud) is never called. Every result in this
  repository is computed locally. gcloud is documented - extensively, in
  99_reference/CLI_REFERENCE.md - and running any of those commands against
  a project of your own is your business, under Google's terms, not this
  repository's.

ON WHAT THE NUMBERS ARE WORTH

Prices, quotas, discount rates and permission counts in this repository are
REPRESENTATIVE MODELS, labelled as such where they appear. They are chosen so
the shape of a decision is visible, and they move. Nothing here is a quote,
and no part of it is a substitute for Google's own pricing calculator or
documentation.
